AUDIO: 'This is Canvas UI, an open-source library of tasteful HTML and Canvas and WebGL components, all framework agnostic and installable with shadcn, so you own the code. This has some of the coolest components and effects that I\'ve seen in a while, and I just wanted to share'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that. And I\'m also super excited to see HTML and Canvas actually getting used, as it could seriously make the future of the web actually fun. And it also has a cool use case that I think a lot of people look over. Let\'s check it out. So here on my documentation, you can'

[00:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'find all of the 33 components this library currently has. And I\'ll just start out with the ASCII object, which is the first one that comes up. You can see it\'s this really cool rubber duck here, but it\'s built out of ASCII objects. But it still maintains that 3D look, and we can pan this in 3D as well.'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
